Z||000002||Spektrum-87GT||11-20-2001||09:53 PM||||a couple different routes you can take... if you want to go digital, jc whitney sells a nice universal one for around 300 bucks. i dont know why they would get dim when you turned on the headlights... another route is the fiero stores white face guages( <A HREF="http://www.fierostore.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fierostore.com</A>  )<P>i'm sure other people will post some ideas||||reg||1
Z||000003||4UMLA1||11-21-2001||11:18 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Spektrum-87GT:<BR><B>a couple different routes you can take... if you want to go digital, jc whitney sells a nice universal one for around 300 bucks. i dont know why they would get dim when you turned on the headlights... another route is the fiero stores white face guages( <A HREF="http://www.fierostore.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fierostore.com</A>  )<P>i'm sure other people will post some ideas</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Thanks for the information.  I got the ones from The Fiero Store and had them put in, BUT, there are a few things that they fail to tell you about those "White Face Gauges," here are the problems that I have had with them:<BR>They dont stay white, in the summer when you have your windows up and the heat gets to them the red die starts to bleed threw them and they turn light red.<BR>When you turn on your lights at night, you can hardly even see them, I guess it is because they are so thick, that is the major problem.<BR>Other than that, they look fine, but if I had it to do over, I would haver neer taken that "Cheap" route.<P>||||reg||14
